{
  "case_id": "2007-06-457",
  "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul Stern, on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has left to the States and encouraged them to deal with the significant public health problem of youth access to tobacco. The question presented is whether the FAAA Act nonetheless preempts the two State laws before the Court and those laws that ensure that tobacco shipped into the State of Maine does not end up in the hands of our children."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But the Synar -- I don't have it in front of me, but the Synar Amendment refers to -- to a number of objects of State legislation that would be required, but it doesn't say anything about regulating transportation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But I don't really see why\nthe States have -- have a different interest in\nregulating shipment of tobacco to minors than they would\na variety of other substances that could be harmful to\nminors or contraband in general. And you don't try to\nregulate any of those?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. STERN",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STERN: The Federal Government has a\nrole with respect to the shipment of explosives, but it\nhas no role with respect to the shipment of tobacco."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Before you do that,\nMs. Brinkmann, would you tell us how alcohol is\nhandled, because that is, as I understand it, that's by\nvirtue of the 24th Amendment State regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. BRINKMANN",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BRINKMANN: To your first question, just\nto complete it, Your Honor, at JA-96 there's an\nadmission that it's a two-dollar cost to research a\npackage. There it's for the addressee, but it would be\nthe same for the shipper. And if you had to do that for\nthe 16 million packages going to Maine a year just\nthrough UPS, it would be $32 million a year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why is it that knowledge requirements have a different preemption analysis?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could the State do it beyond the Federal requirement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Before you get into that, do we have to hold -- assuming we agree with you -- do we have to hold that the knowing requirement of the first sentence is okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0002-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think there's no question that the State of Maine could not require carriers to obtain a license to deliver tobacco products and condition that upon the carrier's service complying with the mandates of State law, that that would be a law that relates to the carrier's service. Now, Maine maintains that its law is saved from preemption because of two distinctions: One, it that is adopted with a health rather than economic purpose, and because it operates directly on the shipper rather than the carrier."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If one of the big carriers decides for its own business purposes to offer a service that complied with the Maine law, would that have the effect of \"un-pre-empting\" the Maine law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the first condition, and the package is clearly labeled, aren't there some commodities where UPS does have to pay attention to the label?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But won't the name of the shipper be in their computer program?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thank you, Your Honor. Beginning with the last series of questions, if the Court looks at pages 100 to 102 of the joint appendix, the Court will see that UPS has a computer dial-up system which allows it to keep track of, and provide alerts for, shippers' addresses and consignees, as well as they can keep track of what is called an SIC code which is with respect to commodities. And they can keep track of tobacco commodities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-457",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b77c85f77a9015c09bf1efc7bd797e30ed1b0d78fe37d2a8e0fc09ede40a9af",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b77c85f77a9-0002-0010",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
